# ttychatter.ncurses changelog

## 0.10.2

### Added
- `Shift+O` / uppercase `O` in the model browser to cycle sort methods in reverse.
- Choice-list selector for options that have a finite set of legal values.
- `ctrl_enter` as a recognized `SEND_INPUT` choice in options and config parsing.
- Expanded maintainer commentary around terminal-edge drawing safety and option choice handling.

### Changed
- `SEND_INPUT` is no longer edited as arbitrary free text in the options screen; it is selected from supported values.
- Model browser sort cycling now supports both forward (`o`) and reverse (`O`) direction.
- Model sort choices now consistently include `favorites`, `api`, `name`, `display`, `input-desc`, and `output-desc`.
- Help/man page text now documents `Ctrl+Enter` as terminal-dependent instead of guaranteed.

### Fixed
- More menu/list screens now consistently accept vim-style `j`/`k` navigation.
- Prevented invalid free-form `SEND_INPUT` values from being saved through the options form.

### Notes
- `Ctrl+Enter` support depends on the terminal emulator. Many terminals report it as ordinary Enter.
- The embedded editor idea was not implemented because embedding real external editors inside a curses subwindow would require pseudo-terminal integration and is outside this release.

## 0.10.0

### Added
- OpenRouter-first provider migration for the ncurses client.
- XDG-style default directories for config, sessions, attachments, and model cache.
- `--resume` support for bare names, `.log` filenames, and explicit paths.
- Model-browser search by typed string.
- Persistent model favorites/bookmarks.
- Favorite-aware model sorting.
- Session-browser New Chat action.
- Session-browser Delete action with confirmation.
- `SEND_INPUT` config key.
- `PROMPT_SESSION_NAME` config key.
- `CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES` config key.
- Short code blocks stay inline; long code blocks become attachments.

### Changed
- `safe_addstr` no longer clips one character from every right edge; it only reserves the final cell on the bottom row.
- AI transcript messages are dimmed while user messages remain normal/white by default.
- Model-list refresh requires explicit confirmation before connecting to OpenRouter.
- Cached model list is preferred in the model menu.
- Startup notice now includes a temporary system explanation for the message list window.

### Documentation
- Updated flat-layout man page and README for OpenRouter, XDG paths, and model-browser behavior.
